  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Bidding**: Dealer's opponent speaks first. Can 'Take' (accept passed card), 'Schmeiss' (offer re-deal), or 'Pass'. If both pass, second round allows naming any suit. 2. **Melding**: Before playing to the first trick, announce sequences. Only the best one counts. 3. **Play**: Follow suit. Must Trump if void. Must Over-trump if possible. 4. **Winning**: If Maker scores > Opponent, points stand. If Maker fails (BÃªte), Opponent gets ALL points.",
    Player: "1. **Bidding**: Dealer's opponent speaks first. Can 'Take' (accept passed card), 'Schmeiss' (offer re-deal), or 'Pass'. If both pass, second round allows naming any suit. 2. **Melding**: Before playing to the first trick, announce sequences. Only the best one counts. 3. **Play**: Follow suit. Must Trump if void. Must Over-trump if possible. 4. **Winning**: If Maker scores > Opponent, points stand. If Maker fails (BÃªte), Opponent gets ALL points.",
    objective: 'Score more points than the opponent to win the deal. Usually played to 501.',
    gameplay: "1. **Bidding**: Dealer's opponent speaks first. Can 'Take' (accept passed card), 'Schmeiss' (offer re-deal), or 'Pass'. If both pass, second round allows naming any suit. 2. **Melding**: Before playing to the first trick, announce sequences. Only the best one counts. 3. **Play**: Follow suit. Must Trump if void. Must Over-trump if possible. 4. **Winning**: If Maker scores > Opponent, points stand. If Maker fails (BÃªte), Opponent gets ALL points.",
    keyRules: [
      "The 'Dix' (7 of Trumps) can be swapped for the turned trump card if the trump was accepted in the first round.",
      'Melds are declared *before* the first trick is complete, revealing information.',
      "You do not need to win a trick to score 'Bella', but you DO need to win a trick to score Sequences.",
